cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SoloDuet in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SoloDuet: single Jacobi ellipsoid vs. Roche contact-binary light-curve discrimination"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sonnett"
    given-names: "S."
    email: "ssonnett@psi.edu"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-16"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/SarahSonnett/SoloDuet"
abstract: >-
  SoloDuet fits both a single rotating triaxial ellipsoid (constrained to the
  fluid-equilibrium Jacobi sequence, or optionally unconstrained) and a
  tidally locked Roche contact/close-binary model to an asteroid rotational
  light curve, and evaluates which model the data statistically prefer,
  following the methodology of Lacerda & Jewitt (2007, AJ 133, 1393).
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Lacerda"
        given-names: "P."
      - family-names: "Jewitt"
        given-names: "D. C."
    title: "Densities of Solar System Objects from Their Rotational Light Curves"
    journal: "The Astronomical Journal"
    volume: 133
    start: 1393
    year: 2007
    doi: "10.1086/511772"
